  "notes": "TCL 65\" C7K QD-Mini LED Google TV, Brazil (device G08, model \"Smart TV Pro\", MediaTek mt5896)\nAndroid 14 (Google TV), firmware UTT2.250416.001, product G08_4K_GB, locale pt-BR.\nSame G08 board and build as examples/tcl-c755-google-tv; that list was the starting point.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/tcl-65c7k-google-tv/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/tcl-65c7k-google-tv/debloat.txt com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx. Live TV / HDMI app: com.tcl.tv.\nKeep: tv.mopa.ginga (Ginga, the Brazilian broadcast middleware for TV aberta), com.tcl.tv,\ncom.tcl.tvinput, com.tcl.suspension (the Input button's source panel), com.tcl.inputmethod.international\n(the keyboard), com.google.android.tv.remote.service, com.dolby.*, and the other TCL/MediaTek system\nservices listed as kept in examples/tcl-c755-google-tv.\nApplied and verified on a real unit on 2026-10-21 (same day, not yet lived with for days): HDMI\nswitching, TV aberta (Ginga) and the launcher as Home over Wi-Fi. Chromecast not tested yet.\nsetupwraith owned the saved Wi-Fi network: forget and re-join it in Settings first (it then belongs\nto com.android.tv.settings), or disable.sh skips it and Home falls back to its RecoveryActivity.\ndreamx kept on purpose (the owner likes the ambient screensaver).\nWireless debugging only switches on over Wi-Fi: on Ethernet the toggle flips straight back off.\nPair once over Wi-Fi, run `adb tcpip 5555`, and port 5555 then answers on either network until reboot.\nTCL tracking and analytics",
